Package: sg-shell
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, wine-sg (>= 10.0-156) | wine, fonts-inter, fonts-liberation, xdotool,
         fonts-crosextra-carlito, fonts-crosextra-caladea, fonts-cascadia-code,
         fonts-noto-cjk,
         python3, sg-session (>= 0.1.0-91), xterm, lxterminal, libglib2.0-bin,
         librsvg2-bin, xdg-utils
Description: Stained Glass OS shell panels (Start menu, Control Panel, Task Manager)
 Windows 10-style panels for the surfaces Wine's explorer does not provide:
 the Start menu (sg-start), the Control Panel (sg-control), Remote Desktop
 Connection (sg-mstsc) and gpresult. The taskbar's appearance is handled in
 wine-sg, not here. Panels install as PE programs under
 /usr/libexec/stained-glass/shell.
 .
 The Control Panel's administrative changes (computer name, domain, local
 accounts, time zone, update checks) are made by sg-admind, a root service
 that acts only on requests from the elevated SYSTEM account.

Package: sg-office
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, sg-shell (= ${source:Version}), wine-sg | wine, sg-office-editors
Description: SG Office for Stained Glass OS (documents, spreadsheets, presentations)
 The office suite's place in Stained Glass OS: SG Office Documents,
 Spreadsheets and Presentations in the Start menu, the default programs for
 Microsoft Office's file types (until the user installs another suite) and
 Settings > Default apps rows. They start SG Office's editors, our own suite
 based on ONLYOFFICE (package sg-office-editors).

Package: sg-pdf
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, sg-shell (= ${source:Version}), wine-sg | wine, sg-session (>= 0.1.0-139)
Breaks: sg-shell (<< 0.1.0-138)
Replaces: sg-shell (<< 0.1.0-138)
Description: SG PDF for Stained Glass OS: view, edit, fill, sign and organize PDFs
 SG PDF is Stained Glass OS's PDF program: a viewer (continuous, single and
 two-page views, thumbnails, bookmarks, attachments, find, dark pages, read
 out loud, print) and an editor with the familiar professional PDF editor's
 tools -- edit text and pictures, comments with replies and stamps, Fill &
 Sign, Prepare Form (fields found on a paper form; formats, calculations),
 certificate signatures and their validation, true redaction, organize
 pages, headers and footers, watermarks, Bates numbers, text recognition
 for scans, Create PDF from files, office documents and the scanner,
 export, combine, protect and reduce file size. It is the default program
 for PDF files, on the Windows side and for Linux programs.
 .
 The Windows program is ours; MuPDF (python3-pymupdf) in sg-session's sg-pdf
 does the PDF work, OCRmyPDF and Tesseract the text recognition.
